{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1475161018,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50ODA3MTM0NTkx"},"added":[],"removed":["conference agenda item"]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1475869481,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1MjM0NDA2OQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/925#issuecomment-252344069"},"message":"Ok, I will address this one by providing `-w,--wanted` which could be either\n- one of the [standard annex groups](https://git-annex.branchable.com/preferred_content/standard_groups/)\n- few of our custom groups\n  - `backup-unrestricted` -- `not metadata=distribution-restrictions=*`\n  - `unique` -- to push derived data (the one present only locally) mostly, but somewhat simplistic since would be just `copies=1` (might consult @joeyh on optimal one).  \n  - `unique-unrestricted` -- as unique but with constrained restriction, which we could advise on while defining a sibling if there is any file with 'distribution-restrictions'\n- and if not matching any of those -- taken as a [preferred content](https://git-annex.branchable.com/preferred_content/) expression  (or should we be kosher and make those separate?  `--wanted-group` and `--wanted` staying more in line with annex?)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1476715045,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1NDIyNjA3Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/925#issuecomment-254226073"},"message":"so may be specification (to fight combinatorics) should accept multiple entries and also \"unify\" with notions for what git supposed to push, e.g.:\n- `nodata` (default), alternatives: `backup`, `unique`\n- `unrestricted` (default), alternatives: `norestrictions`\n- `allbranches` (default), alternatives: `branches=branch1*,branch2*` (may be talk about refs, but then would need `tags/` and `heads/` prefixes ... and `alltags`?\n\nand this settings should be stored in non-persistent config for that remote so they could be picked up later by sub-dataset without requiring to retype them on commandline","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1478576422,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDg1MDkzODQ4MA=="},"added":["conference agenda item"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1478576894,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1OTAzODMzMw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/925#issuecomment-259038333"},"message":"we really need to boil down common use-cases... may be one switch indeed would not be sufficient and we need `--publish-data`, `--publish-branches`, `--publish-tags` which, if no argument provided would assume `nodata` for data, `*` for branches, and `*` for tags.  Then, when values are provided , act accordingly (e.g. would be the list of branches, tags, and custom selection for data as outlined above).  May be we could allow for a shortcut `--publish-all` which would be identical to `--publish-data=backup --publish-branches=* --publish-tags=*`.  Those settings in turn would be set within corresponding `remote.{}.datalad-publish-...` configs within `.git/config`, similar to how `remote.{}.datalad-publish-depends` now is set.  Saving those would allow for \"publish -r\", if reaching a sub-dataset which has no remote yet, to figure out all (?) settings from its parent and invoke correct `create-sibling`, which would simplify life of maintainers of collections of datasets ;)\n@bpoldrack  and @mih - what do you think?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1478577462,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI1OTAzOTQ2Nw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/925#issuecomment-259039467"},"message":"FWIW, not specifying `--publish-branches` would in effect not provide any setting (recorded as empty in the config to be inherited by sub-datasets) thus making it behave as regular git repository, where the branch is pushed only to the tracking remote.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486665337,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3ODczMTcyMQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/925#issuecomment-278731721"},"message":"Will try to play with preferred content some time soon. I believe a joint brainstorming session would be helpful before anyone starts to write this down.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1486676532,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3ODc4MzA2MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/925#issuecomment-278783060"},"message":"tomorrow during hangout @mih? ;)","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1486989243,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDI3OTM3Njk3MA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/925#issuecomment-279376970"},"message":"We indeed need to keep in mind that we have to handle annex content and git content. My current concept\n\n`remote.\u003cname\u003e.datalad-publish`\n\n- `all` -\u003e `git push --mirror`, and copy all data (manually in the git annex sense)\n- `none` -\u003e refuse to publish anything (pull only remote; safety measure)\n- `auto` -\u003e let git annex decide (`annex copy --auto`; could be configured by create-sibling, or obtained via an update of the git-annex branch from any other location)\n\nWe should stick with `remote.\u003cname\u003e.push` to configure what Git content to push in more complicated cases.\n\nI am unsure what `create-sibling` should use as default setup when nothing is specified. I am learning towards `auto`, so that restrictions coming with a dataset are obeyed by default. But I don't know enough about preferred content yet to be able to judge that.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1523026589,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE0OlVubGFiZWxlZEV2ZW50MTU2MTA5MzI4NA=="},"added":[],"removed":["conference agenda item"]}]}